{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 487edd74c37aae85f73a2eca16ad3482c9301130. Revision 2 repairs the original five synthetic controls: malformed billed quantities are incomplete, a full namespace page without metadata continues, provider message text is omitted, and the preceding minute is included in storage queries. All five independently pass on this head. Three further code defects and one incomplete deliverable remain.\n\n[P2] Keep invocation evidence inside the requested window — packages/room/measure/rows.mjs:230. queryWorkerRows passes sampledFrom to namespaceRows, which uses the same start for both datasets. An invocation at 11:59:30 can therefore make the requested 12:00–13:00 window pass even when no invocation occurred in that window. My fake filters by the transmitted start and returns the earlier invocation plus a storage sample: the candidate returns pass instead of incomplete. The padding is necessary for start-stamped storage intervals, but it must not expand the evidence window used to decide that the requested run occurred. Use separate storage and invocation start variables, preserve from for invocation evidence and output totals, and cover this in both query APIs as applicable. This is the explicit absent-invocation fail-closed obligation in request 8bd623cc.\n\n[P2] Redact the complete error before truncating it — packages/room/measure/rows.mjs:117–119. safeMessage slices at 1,000 characters before replacing the known analytics token. A transport message with 985 ordinary characters followed by the supplied opaque credential retains its first 15 characters, because the whole credential is no longer present and there need not be a Bearer prefix. This partial credential is then saved/printed/posted through the same report boundary; it violates the stated never-token-text promise even though it is not the complete usable credential. My synthetic assertion fails on the unchanged head. Apply credential and syntax redaction before the final output bound, and cover credentials crossing the bound and both exception/report paths. No real credential was used or disclosed.\n\n[P2] Reject an owned namespace that cannot be attributed — packages/room/measure/rows.mjs:149–151. An entry whose script explicitly matches this Worker is silently discarded if its ID or class is missing. If the three required classes are otherwise represented, discovery and the gate still pass while the omitted namespace's costs are unknown. My synthetic list supplies those three valid entries and an additional owned Room entry without an ID; the candidate returns a passing report rather than incomplete. Required-class existence is not evidence that every owned namespace was accounted for. Treat malformed owned entries as incomplete; continue ignoring entries positively owned by a different Worker. The provider's namespace schema makes ID and class optional, so this is a shape the caller must handle rather than silently counting it as nothing. See the primary [Cloudflare namespace API schema](https://developers.cloudflare.com/api/resources/durable_objects/subresources/namespaces/methods/list/).\n\n[P2] Complete the commissioned measurements before claiming part 1 is done — packages/room/measure/README.md:8,235–238; packages/room/measure/results/row-costs-2026-10-02.md:57,62,64–65. Request 8bd623cc explicitly commissions physical rows written and read for one check, an idle alarm tick, a pending-pin alarm tick and policy activation with N proposals. Those remain unisolated, inferred or derived; the honest caveats are valuable, but “all three parts are done” cannot satisfy the full deliverable. Add isolation controls and billing evidence for the requested operations, including both read and write counts, recorded windows/namespaces and separation of activation from landing. Keep these gaps visibly open until that evidence exists. The separately commissioned idle-write fix may precede clean measurement; estimates do not remove these operations from scope. I do not flag the existing idle-write storm as a defect introduced by this measurement patch.\n\nArchitecture: this is an ordinary Artroom measurement/CLI and acceptance-gate change, with proposed application budgets and an inert scheduled workflow. It changes no Gitseq kernel, storage, host or application-profile contract and does not adopt a new protocol or provider capability. The effective planner-to-builder request, builder promise, checker invitation/promise and all 16 exact-head artifacts were independently inspected. Actual source base is main 77d2e6c5; the 11 unchanged artifact paths are byte-identical to caefe17d, and the five-file repair delta was read in full. Current main has since advanced to 99cc4044 with diagnostics; landing must preserve those intervening changes, rather than treating an older base as introduced deletions. No landing or deployment is approved by this verdict.\n\nSecurity: using account analytics and script read permissions is appropriate for this read-only observer; known credentials should cross only the fetch boundary. Provider error metadata improves confidentiality, but the remaining truncation defect still exposes credential text. Unknown namespace evidence must not authorize a passing cost gate. My checks used synthetic responses only: no provider reads, credentials, deployments, webhook delivery or operations on other actors' resources. Turning on the scheduled workflow and enforcing budgets remain explicit future work.\n\nSimplification: keep one validated billing boundary and separate the requested invocation window from the storage coverage window. Use one safe error helper, with redaction before output bounding, and fail incomplete whenever attribution is missing. Preserve the single shared sampling-start helper without presenting an unverified maximum interval as a hard provider guarantee. Recorded non-Room cadence sometimes exceeds 60 seconds; cadence alone does not prove interval duration. My additional 63-second interval stress case fails under that assumed interval model, but I do not file it as a confirmed provider defect. Establish the coverage assumption or retain it explicitly as a limitation before promising edges can never undercount. FIFO and alarm constants are proposed budgets, not implemented runtime caps; retry warm-up/bursts and workload assumptions must be considered when request 99782949 enforces them.\n\nEvidence: clean detached /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v2; npm ci, root typecheck and Room test:node exit 0, 165 passed. In /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v2-guards all 14 supplied revision-2 mutants independently fail named runtime tests, zero syntax failures; restored rows/budgets tests pass 27/27 and tracked checkout is clean. Source diff --check passes. The original five checker controls pass 5/5. Three additional controls fail at runtime for the findings above; a fourth is the explicitly qualified interval-model stress case. Scripts/logs: /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v2-controls.mjs and -controls.log; /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v2-extra-controls.mjs and -extra-controls.log; /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v2-mutants.py, -mutants.log and /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v2-mut/results.json. Prior caefe17d root tests independently passed 1,865 with one skipped, including Room 160 Node/403 workerd; the workerd suite was not rerun for this five-file measurement repair, whose packages/room/src contents are unchanged.\n\nOffline measurement checks: the two saved per-act tables reproduce all supplied room/write/read/baseline/act and Registry/Publisher columns with zero mismatches using windowTable. The saved JSON omits other Room samples and invocation rows, so I do not claim to independently recompute those columns. The recorded clean smoke total 2,284 equals its saved object sum, maximum 508, and passes the current 9,200/2,100 ceilings retrospectively; its recorded gate used earlier provisional ceilings. The earlier 16:35 run has failed cleanup and six unresolved records, while the 17:23 run failed an obligation; neither is represented as the clean acceptance run. No fresh live billing measurement or hourly-query result is claimed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da0e0fb31f4047f6905fbd2972c534c4f53f36d5","binding":"assigned","head":"487edd74c37aae85f73a2eca16ad3482c9301130","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:47696d3cd6af24be5f9e5b7dd157fe551d9596cc\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f3d305c3d4defed39ac3e9c9b8f7326e239fba7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:47696d3cd6af24be5f9e5b7dd157fe551d9596cc","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}